---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Panel from '../components/Panel.astro';
import { TOOLS } from '../data/tools';

const tool = TOOLS.find((t) => t.href === '/privacy')!;

/** Rendered at build time, so the date never goes stale. */
const lastUpdated = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
---

<Base title={tool.title} description={tool.meta} tool={tool} keywords={tool.keywords}>
  <!-- ============================ Hero ============================ -->
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="hero__text">
      <p class="label label--accent">Legal · Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="hero__lead">
        Every tone, sweep and recording is generated in your browser, and no audio you play, record or open ever
        leaves your device. This page explains the one exception to a site with no accounts, no advertising and no
        tracking of you as a person: aggregate page-view statistics from Google Analytics.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="hero__aside">
      <div class="notice notice--info">
        <span class="notice__icon" aria-hidden="true">i</span>
        <p class="notice__body">
          Last updated: <span class="mono">{lastUpdated}</span>. This page is short on purpose. There is little to
          disclose.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Panel eyebrow="Privacy" title="The short version">
    <div class="prose-tech">
      <p>
        Nothing is uploaded. Every tone, sweep, noise signal and click is synthesised locally by the Web Audio API in
        your browser. When you use the <a href="/voice-recorder">voice recorder</a>, your microphone audio is captured
        and processed in the browser only and is never transmitted. When you use the
        <a href="/pitch-shifter">pitch shifter</a> or <a href="/time-stretcher">time stretcher</a>, the audio file you
        open is read and processed in the browser only and is never transmitted. There is no server that could receive
        any of it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Panel>

  <Panel eyebrow="Detail" title="What is and is not collected">
    <div class="prose-tech">
      <h2>Accounts, advertising and tracking</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No accounts.</strong> There is nothing to register, log in to, or pay for.</li>
        <li><strong>No cookies of our own.</strong> The site sets no first-party cookies.</li>
        <li><strong>No advertising.</strong> No ads, no sponsorship, no advertising code.</li>
        <li><strong>No behavioural profiling.</strong> No pixel, no fingerprinting script, no cross-site profile of you.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Page-view statistics.</strong> Google Analytics measures which pages are visited, in aggregate. It is
          the only third-party script on the site, and the detail is in the next section.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        The site loads Google Analytics 4 (measurement ID <code>G-FK8YJ3XSX7</code>) so that the people who build and
        pay for it can see which tools are used and which pages are worth improving. It collects standard aggregate
        data: the page you viewed, the referring page, an approximate location derived from your IP address, and your
        device, browser and screen information. It does not receive anything you type, play or record, and it cannot
        see your audio.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Cookies.</strong> Google sets first-party cookies such as <code>_ga</code> and
          <code>_ga_FK8YJ3XSX7</code> to distinguish one visit from another. They contain a randomly generated
          identifier, not your name.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>IP addresses.</strong> IP anonymisation is enabled. Google states that it does not log or store the
          full IP address for this property.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control.</strong> If your browser sends either signal, the analytics
          script is not loaded at all and no request is made to Google.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Where the data goes.</strong> Google Ireland Limited and Google LLC process it as an independent
          controller. See Google's own
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a> and
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses data from sites</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Opting out.</strong> Block third-party scripts or cookies for this site in your browser, use a
          content blocker, or install Google's
          <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Analytics opt-out add-on</a>. The site works
          normally with analytics blocked; nothing here depends on it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Local development is excluded.</strong> The script is only added to production builds, so the dev
          server never includes it. Serving a production build locally (for example with <code>npm run preview</code>,
          or a browser preview extension) does send hits, so block it if that matters to you.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Definitely not collected</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No audio.</strong> Nothing you play, speak, record or open as a file is transmitted anywhere.</li>
        <li><strong>No text you type.</strong> The voice generator's text, frequency entries and settings stay local.</li>
        <li><strong>No microphone data.</strong> The recorder's stream is processed in a local audio graph and closed when you stop.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Nothing is uploaded</h2>
      <p>
        All audio is generated and processed on your device. This applies to the microphone input on the
        <a href="/voice-recorder">voice recorder</a> and to any file you open in the
        <a href="/pitch-shifter">pitch shifter</a> or <a href="/time-stretcher">time stretcher</a>. Processing happens
        in a local audio graph, and the microphone stream is closed when you stop recording. No audio data is sent
        anywhere.
      </p>

      <h2>What is stored locally on your device</h2>
      <p>
        The site keeps a small amount of information in your browser's <code>localStorage</code> so that settings
        survive a reload. It stays on your device and is not transmitted.
      </p>
      <table class="table-tech">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Key</th><th>What it holds</th><th>Why</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="mono">sg.master.v1</td>
            <td>The master volume slider position, a number from 0 to 100.</td>
            <td>So the site level is the same when you come back.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="mono">sg.hearing.v1</td>
            <td>Your results from the <a href="/hearing-test">hearing test</a>, if you choose to save them.</td>
            <td>So the log survives a reload. It is only written if you use that page.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        Everything of ours is keyed under <code>sg.</code> To clear it, use your browser's settings to delete site data
        or storage for <code>soundgenerator.app</code>. Clearing it resets the volume and removes any saved hearing-test
        log; the site works normally afterwards. Clearing site data also removes the Google Analytics cookies described
        above.
      </p>

      <h2>Third parties</h2>
      <p>
        Google Analytics is the only third-party script, font or resource the pages load. Everything else is served
        from this domain. Three things outside the site may still apply.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google Analytics.</strong> Covered in full in the section above, including how to block or opt out of it.</li>
        <li><strong>Hosting server logs.</strong> The static files are served by a hosting provider, which may keep
          ordinary server logs such as your IP address and the time of the request, as any web host does. Those logs
          are outside this site's control.</li>
        <li><strong>Speech synthesis voices.</strong> The <a href="/voice-generator">voice generator</a> uses the
          speech voices installed by your browser or operating system. How those voices are provided, which may include
          remote synthesis on some platforms, is governed by your browser and OS vendor, not by this site.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        There is no account and no profile of you to request or delete. For the aggregate statistics described above,
        you can object by blocking the analytics script or by sending the Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control
        signal, both of which stop it loading. For questions or requests, write to the address in the contact section.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        The site has no accounts and collects no personal information about individuals, so it can be used by anyone.
        Where a young user operates the generators, adult supervision is sensible for the same reason it is for any
        audio equipment: loud tones can damage hearing.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the revised text will appear on this page with a new date at the top. The date is
        generated when the site is built, so it always reflects the published version.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Write to <a href="mailto:hello@tehnika.mk">hello@tehnika.mk</a> with any privacy question. The
        address is also listed in plain text as <code>hello@tehnika.mk</code>.
      </p>
      <p>
        See the <a href="/about">about page</a> for how the tools work, and the
        <a href="/theory">acoustic theory</a> page for the physics behind them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Panel>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.5fr) minmax(260px, 1fr);
    gap: 20px;
    align-items: start;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .hero { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3.2vw, 2.1rem);
    margin: 6px 0 8px;
  }
  .hero__lead {
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
    max-width: 68ch;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 14.5px;
  }
  .notice__body { margin: 0; }
  .prose-tech table { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
</style>
